# === Secrets — NEVER commit ===
.env
*.token
data/.domain_token

# === Runtime / regenerated data (keep ONLY curated inputs) ===
data/*
!data/catalysts.json
!data/policies.json
!data/id_forecast.json
!data/sa2_lga.json
!data/sa2_gccsa.json
!data/vg_yoy.json
!data/rents.json
!data/nsw_sales.json
!data/news_feed.json
# news_feed.json is a committed SEED: GitHub Actions' datacenter IPs can't reach several
# commercial RSS feeds (YIP, realestate, RenewEconomy, Sourceable), so the CI run alone would
# show only the gov/infra feeds. Committing the full local pull keeps the News tab multi-source
# (incl. Your Investment Property); the daily run MERGES fresh items onto it where reachable.
# Refresh with `python3 -m propintel.news_feed` + commit, like the other caches.
# (everything else in data/ — suburb_analysis.json, *.db,
#  sa2_centroids.json, logs, digests — is regenerated by the pipeline)
# id_forecast.json (.id council forecasts, ~annual refresh) and sa2_lga.json
# (SA2→LGA, static geography) are committed caches the pipeline READS — regenerate
# occasionally with `python3 -m propintel.id_forecast`, not in the daily run.

# === Generated report output (rebuilt by `report` / the Action) ===
reports/emerging-growth-report.html
reports/_*.html

# === Caches / envs / OS ===
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
.cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store

# Copyrighted / third-party documents — never publish
*.pdf

# Local Claude Code config — not for the public repo
.claude/
